<title>JAPAN: Nissan, Hino down on higher yen.</title>
<headline>Nissan, Hino down on higher yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nissan Motor Co Ltd and Hino Motors Ltd slipped on Thursday afternoon, discouraged by the yen's climb against the dollar, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0539 GMT, the share price of Nissan Motor was down 15 yen at 829 yen. Volume was 2.244 million shares.</p>
<p>Hino Motor's share price fell by 20 yen to 970 yen, on turnover of 245,000 shares.</p>
<p>As of 0544 GMT, the dollar stood at 112.35/40 yen, against its New York close of 113.92/02 yen on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A strong yen slashes export income and makes Japanese products less competitive abroad.</p>
</text>
